"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/15533"} "Georges Maton"] ", and the Dutch team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/15283"} "Bernard Leene"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/15954"} "Henk Ooms"] " racing the Italians " [:a {:href "/athletes/15286"} "Carlo Leguti"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/15350"} "Bruno Loatti"] ". The first semi was close, with Germany defeating the French by just over a wheel, but, in the second semi, the Netherlands easily defeated Italy."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final saw Germany, clearly the best team in the event, win the gold medal in two straight races, both by fairly comfortable margins. France defeated Italy for the bronze medal. For the Netherlands, Bernard Leene was competing in his third straight Olympics on the tandem, having won gold in " [:a {:href "/results/153389"} "1928"] " with " [:a {:href "/athletes/16987"} "Daan van Dijk"] ", and placing fourth in " [:a {:href "/results/153441"} "1932"] ". Bronze medalist Pierre Georget also won a silver in the " [:a {:href "/results/153461"} "kilometre time trial at Berlin"] ", and in 1936 and 1937 would place second at the World Championships in the match sprint."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "R1 Rep"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/14838"} "Ernst Ihbe"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/15373"} "Carl Lorenz"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "11.6 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "11.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "11.0 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "2 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/15283"} "Bernard Leene"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/15954"} "Henk Ooms"]